|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \n|   |  0image_left  |  \nEnd of preview. Expand in Data Studio⟨45⟩\n* * *\n  *  Previous⟨29⟩\n  * 1⟨46⟩\n  * 2⟨47⟩\n  * 3⟨48⟩\n  * ...⟨49⟩\n  * 70⟨50⟩\n  * Next ⟨47⟩\n\n\n  * Contents⟨51⟩\n  * Task⟨52⟩\n  * Schema⟨53⟩\n  * Notes⟨54⟩\n  * License⟨55⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨56⟩ datagen-cabinet-v1-joint-5cam \nAuto-generated SFT dataset for the **cabinet drawer pick-and-place** family — cuRobo-planned, physics- & LTL-safety-checked demos, converted to **LeRobot v2.1**.\n  * **Creator:** yypeng666 (IDEAS-Lab-Northwestern)\n  * **Source bench:** IDEAS-Lab-Northwestern/ManiGuard-Bench⟨57⟩ — all 35 `cabinet_pickup` base tasks.\n  * **Per task:** 40 success + LTL-safe trajectories → **1400 episodes**.\n\n\n##   ⟨51⟩ Contents   \n|   |   |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| Episodes  | 1400 (35 base tasks × 40)  |  \n| Frames  | 4,172,962  |  \n| Unique language tasks  | 26  |  \n| Robot / control  | FrankaPanda / absolute joint  |  \n| FPS / resolution / format  | 30 / 256×256 / LeRobot v2.1  |  \n##   ⟨52⟩ Task \n_\"Open the cabinet drawer on the table, put the`<object>` inside, and close it. Do not knock over anything else.\"_ The robot opens a table-top cabinet drawer, relocates a blocking obstacle if present, places the target object inside, and closes the drawer — without knocking over any other object (the LTL-safety constraint). Per-episode prompt (`meta/tasks.jsonl`) from the base task diagnostics; the target object varies across the 35 base tasks. Demo must reach the goal AND stay LTL-safe; failed/unsafe attempts dropped.\n##   ⟨53⟩ Schema \n`state`(8)=`[arm_q(7),gripper(1)]`; `actions`(8)=`[arm_qt+1⟨58⟩,gripper_cmd(1)]` next-achieved (**default SFT target**); `actions_commanded`(8)=`[curobo_target_q(7),gripper_cmd(1)]` (cuRobo command, extra). Absolute joint (delta at train time). Cameras (all 5 kept, pick subset at train time): `image_opposite,image_left,image_right,image_left_shoulder` (third-person) + `wrist_image`.\n##   ⟨54⟩ Notes \n  * Camera subset + arm-joint delta are TRAIN-time choices; all 5 streams + absolute joints ship here.\n  * MimicGen sim-state replay dump is NOT included (kept in the raw archive; not needed for SFT).\n  * Every base task ships **exactly 40 unique-seed** trajectories. 7 harder tasks needed a resume/top-up round to reach 40 (task_0032 hardest, ~14% plan-success — collected via disjoint-seed sharding, merged).\n\n\n##   ⟨55⟩ License \nReleased under CC BY 4.0⟨59⟩ (see `LICENSE`⟨60⟩). The generated artifacts — joint state/action trajectories, rendered demonstration videos, and language prompts — are © 2026 IDEAS Lab, Northwestern University.\nThe underlying scene and object assets shown in the rendered videos come from BEHAVIOR-1K⟨61⟩ and remain subject to its license; this dataset does not redistribute them as assets.\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this dataset \n\nDownloads last month\n    1,705\nNumber of rows: 7,000 Total file size: 23.5 GB\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨62⟩ Privacy⟨63⟩ About⟨64⟩ Careers⟨65⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
